<section class="pg on" id="p-about">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>I am an Avionics Engineering graduate of <a href="https://aaub.edu.bd">Aviation and Aerospace University, Bangladesh</a> (BSc, March 2026), with a CGPA of 3.52/4.00. My research interests lie in <b>antennas</b>, <b>radar systems</b>, <b>wireless communications</b> and <b>intelligent sensing</b>.</p>
  <p>My undergraduate thesis involved the design, fabrication and measurement of a compact <b>four-element UWB microstrip MIMO antenna</b>. Building on this foundation, I have contributed to research on patch antennas, <b>OTFS waveforms</b> and <b>integrated sensing and communication (ISAC)</b>. I also serve as a manuscript reviewer for the <b>IEEE Geoscience and Remote Sensing Society</b>. From 2022 to 2025, I worked as a Research Assistant on my university's rocket project, contributing to electrical power system research and development.<button class="more" id="more" type="button" aria-expanded="false">Read more ›</button></p>
  <div id="extra">
    <p>Beyond research, I tutored SSC and HSC students in mathematics and science from 2019 to 2025 and served as Outreach Secretary of the AAUB Drone Club. I have also completed aircraft maintenance training with the Bangladesh Air Force and visited the radar unit of the Civil Aviation Authority of Bangladesh.</p>
  </div>
  <h2>Research focus</h2>
  <p>My current research explores <b>impersonation attacks in UAV swarms</b>, focusing on the security challenges they pose to reliable communication and coordinated swarm operations. I am also working on <b>cellular Integrated Sensing and Communication (ISAC)</b>, particularly how cellular infrastructure can leverage communication signals for environmental sensing. I am interested in using 5G base station downlink transmissions for sensing while maintaining reliable communication services for multiple users. A central challenge is understanding how sensing performance can be preserved and optimized under communication-driven resource allocation and multi-user scheduling constraints.</p>
  <p>I am also exploring <b>Reconfigurable Intelligent Surfaces (RIS)</b> as a means of controlling wireless propagation environments and investigating how RIS-assisted sensing can enhance cellular ISAC systems. My broader goal is to understand and develop adaptive wireless systems that jointly support communication, sensing and intelligent environmental perception.</p>
  <h2>Research interests</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Radar signal processing:</b> Pulse-Doppler radar systems, I/Q signal processing, Moving Target Indication (MTI) and Constant False Alarm Rate (CFAR) detection.</li>
    <li><b>Integrated Sensing and Communication (ISAC):</b> Cellular ISAC, downlink-based sensing, joint sensing and communication, and multi-user resource allocation.</li>
    <li><b>Wireless communications:</b> Wireless system design, signal propagation, emerging wireless networks and communication waveform design.</li>
    <li><b>Reconfigurable Intelligent Surfaces (RIS):</b> Intelligent propagation control, RIS-assisted sensing and RIS-enabled wireless system optimization.</li>
    <li><b>Antennas and microwave engineering:</b> Antenna design, microstrip structures, MIMO systems and electromagnetic performance analysis.</li>
    <li><b>Radar altimeter interference mitigation:</b> SDR-based detection and mitigation of 5G C-band interference in FMCW radar altimeters.</li>
    <li><b>Microwave imaging:</b> Electromagnetic imaging techniques for brain imaging using Vivaldi antennas.</li>
  </ul>
